WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.820
Corpses littered the facility, around twenty
in total.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:08.750
Their massacre had unfolded in a matter of
seconds despite their advanced armor and heavy

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:09.750
weaponry.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:14.389
Their killer, wielding an ancient sword he’d
somehow pulled from thin air, looked upon

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:15.940
them with disdain.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.520
Weak, unworthy opponents.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.210
He breathed heavily - His torso was covered
with bullet wounds and many had punctured

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:24.210
his lungs.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:28.400
It was enough to kill a normal man ten times
over, but not him.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.340
He was the ultimate warrior.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:31.949
The perfect killing machine.

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:36.690
He would need to seek out an enemy more fitting
for his legendary combat skills.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:41.030
He fled from the chamber into a connecting
hallway - where a giant, metal door slammed

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:42.239
shut behind him.

00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:45.440
At the other end of the hall another door
did the same.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.559
He laughed at the thought of someone thinking
he could be trapped so easily and charged

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:50.559
towards it.

00:00:50.559 --> 00:00:54.360
But then, large valves began to open all around
him.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:58.430
Torrents of freezing seawater began pouring
in, filling up the chamber and submerging

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.760
him before he could reach the door.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:06.219
The warrior fought for breath, and he held
it far longer than any mortal man could - especially

00:01:06.219 --> 00:01:10.350
considering the state of his lungs, but water
always wins.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:15.479
He soon gave his last gasp, and floated, lifeless,
in the hallway.

00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:20.289
And soon after his body turned to dust and
disappeared in the briny water.

00:01:20.289 --> 00:01:21.470
But he would be back.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.759
He’d always be back.

00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:25.619
His brother was a different story.

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:30.929
Tall and handsome, with a strange Sumerian
rune tattooed on his forehead, he was practically

00:01:30.929 --> 00:01:35.679
a pacifist and spent most of his days reading,
conversing with the staff, and wandering the

00:01:35.679 --> 00:01:37.950
facility of his own accord.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:41.869
Upon hearing of the latest incident at the
facility, he gave a sigh.

00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:45.020
He knew, on some level, that all of this was
his fault.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.659
It’d been centuries, millennia even.

00:01:47.659 --> 00:01:50.459
But was it too late to make things right?

00:01:50.459 --> 00:01:53.859
Six days later, the two are standing face
to face.

00:01:53.859 --> 00:01:58.469
This meeting had been a long time coming,
but it was always destined to end in blood

00:01:58.469 --> 00:01:59.469
and pain.

00:01:59.469 --> 00:02:04.659
The man with the runic tattoo was unarmed
- the only thing he carried was his regrets.

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:08.939
The warrior, eyes full of burning fury, drew
his sword.

00:02:08.939 --> 00:02:12.200
And not long after, a head hit the floor.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.420
Who are these two strange men?

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.910
And what is the significance of this fatal
meeting?

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:19.780
In our own universe, these two may never meet
again.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:23.799
But that doesn’t mean there isn’t a universe
out there where they will.

00:02:23.799 --> 00:02:27.430
And it is that universe where today’s tale
springs from.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:32.359
The story between these two began a long,
long time ago, when they were both set on

00:02:32.359 --> 00:02:33.430
a course of destruction.

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:39.189
But to learn how these two finally met once
again, we only need to go back a few days.

00:02:39.189 --> 00:02:43.599
While they seem more human than a lot of the
beings under the SCP Foundation’s watchful

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:50.470
eyes, there’s no doubt that these two are
anomalous - they’re known as SCP - 073 and

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:54.989
SCP - 076, but better known as Cain and Able.

00:02:54.989 --> 00:02:58.980
From the name alone, most people with a basic
knowledge of the bible could tell that these

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:03.140
two have a connection, but the particulars
were largely a mystery to the Foundation.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:06.920
They wanted to know how much of the story
was actually true.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:13.269
SCP Researchers approached SCP - 073 - aka,
Cain - and asked if he’d be interested in

00:03:13.269 --> 00:03:16.170
reuniting with his brother one last time.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:22.680
It took Cain three days to answer: Yes, but
on one condition - that he was the only person

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.440
who could abort the mission.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:28.769
The Foundation mulled over this requirement
for three days before the O5 Council finally

00:03:28.769 --> 00:03:31.959
made a decision - Cross-testing approved.

00:03:31.959 --> 00:03:38.030
These two brothers, separated by millennia,
would finally meet again - and the SCP Foundation

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:40.930
would get to watch what happened when they
did.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:45.430
Of course, for safety reasons, the cross-test
would have to take place in 076’s containment

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:49.590
facility - a bedrock chamber two hundred meters
beneath the sea.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:53.900
That would be the closest thing to “safe”
this fateful meeting could ever be.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:59.010
Though safe was really a relative term when
it came to SCP - 076.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:04.139
His escape attempts were as frequent and unpredictable
as they were deadly, and everyone who’d

00:04:04.139 --> 00:04:06.709
ever worked with him knew exactly why.

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:12.019
To the untrained eye, it would seem strange
to create such a complex facility for a three-meter-squared

00:04:12.019 --> 00:04:16.280
stone cube, known as SCP - 076 - 01.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.609
But the cube isn’t what’s being locked
up here.

00:04:18.609 --> 00:04:25.750
The real danger comes from the corpse stored
inside - known as SCP - 076 - 02, but better

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:27.330
known as Able.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:32.460
He’s a lean, olive-skinned man who appears
to be in his late twenties, but his most distinctive

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:37.140
physical feature is the fact he’s covered
in an elaborate network of arcane and occult

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:42.310
tattoos, largely of scowling, demonic faces
- similar to those found on members of the

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:43.310
Yakuza.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:47.720
Whenever Able’s corpse reanimates, as it
does at random intervals, everyone in his

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.789
vicinity is in terrible danger.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:54.199
He’s capable of pulling bladed weapons out
of miniature dimensional rifts that appear

00:04:54.199 --> 00:04:58.250
around him, though he does this so quickly
that it seems as though the weapons are simply

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.639
materializing in his hands.

00:05:00.639 --> 00:05:04.580
Despite the increasingly complex efforts to
contain him, Able has been able to breach

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:10.430
containment and go on brutal rampages multiple
times, killing scores of Foundation personnel

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.800
in the process.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:15.919
Able possesses superhuman strength, speed,
and durability.

00:05:15.919 --> 00:05:19.699
During prior containment breaches, he was
able to shrug off rounds from .50 caliber

00:05:19.699 --> 00:05:20.699
machine guns.

00:05:20.699 --> 00:05:23.139
He’s torn through reinforced steel doors.

00:05:23.139 --> 00:05:27.819
He’s even swatted bullets from both handguns
and assault rifles out of the air with a length

00:05:27.819 --> 00:05:29.389
of steel rebar.

00:05:29.389 --> 00:05:33.979
Only killing him can truly end one of these
rampages - and the Foundation has had to go

00:05:33.979 --> 00:05:38.180
to terrifying lengths in order to achieve
this during past containment breaches.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:43.220
He’s been drowned, asphyxiated, crushed,
burned to death with a thermite grenade directly

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:48.789
inserted into his chest cavity, and even disintegrated
by the activation of the facility’s on-site

00:05:48.789 --> 00:05:50.330
nuclear warhead.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:56.259
This may seem like overkill, but if Able ever
made his way into a major population center,

00:05:56.259 --> 00:06:01.690
the fatalities would be… well, of biblical
proportions.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:06.669
Even death can’t keep him down for long
- his body will rapidly decompose, and reappear

00:06:06.669 --> 00:06:10.300
intact within SCP - 076 - 01.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:15.129
There’s no telling when he’ll reawaken,
and his periods of inactivity can range from

00:06:15.129 --> 00:06:16.949
hours to years.

00:06:16.949 --> 00:06:22.139
Because of this, he must be constantly observed
by guards highly proficient in close combat,

00:06:22.139 --> 00:06:26.880
always ready to go toe to toe with perhaps
the most dangerous melee combatant in history.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:31.580
He’s such a proficient killer that there
was once a project aimed at weaponizing Able,

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:35.190
but this turned out to be a disastrous failure
for the Foundation.

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.909
When they ran out of missions to give him,
Able’s thirst for blood caused him to turn

00:06:38.909 --> 00:06:43.880
his blade on his allies with no remorse, hacking
them up with the same ruthless abandon he

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.229
gave his assigned enemies.

00:06:46.229 --> 00:06:49.629
Interestingly, Able does seem to have a twisted
sense of honour.

00:06:49.629 --> 00:06:53.879
He has a respect for combatants capable of
providing him with a real challenge - and

00:06:53.879 --> 00:06:58.389
has even expressed concern for guards he considers
to be respectable adversaries.

00:06:58.389 --> 00:07:00.380
But don’t be fooled.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:07.290
There is no reasoning with Able - either you
kill him, or he kills you, and trust us, he’s

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:08.970
much better at it than you are.

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:13.710
While he’s often overshadowed by world-ending
anomalies or more talkative mass killers like

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:18.930
SCP - 682, Able is one of the most deadly
creatures known to the Foundation.

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:23.520
Able’s counterpart, 073, is an entirely
different story.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:28.370
Despite his namesake being the first biblical
murderer, this Cain is a far more enigmatic

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:29.370
figure.

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:33.419
A tall man in his early thirties appearing
to be of Middle Eastern descent, he has two

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:38.479
very notable physical characteristics - The
untranslated Sumerian symbol tattooed onto

00:07:38.479 --> 00:07:43.409
his forehead, and the fact that several of
his body parts - namely, his arms, legs, spinal

00:07:43.409 --> 00:07:48.920
cord, and shoulder blades - have been replaced
by mysterious prosthetics of unknown origin.

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:54.439
Unlike Able, Cain is polite, non-confrontational,
articulate, and communicative.

00:07:54.439 --> 00:07:59.409
He’s even allowed to wander the facility
he’s housed in freely, though with certain

00:07:59.409 --> 00:08:00.650
regulations.

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:05.180
Namely that Cain is never permitted to come
into contact with plant life or uncovered

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:06.180
ground.

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:10.729
This is because, in spite of the fact Cain
doesn’t appear to harbor any malicious intent,

00:08:10.729 --> 00:08:16.410
direct contact with him causes plants to wither
and die, and the ground to become infertile.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:20.719
If Cain was ever introduced into a natural
environment again, he could unwittingly cause

00:08:20.719 --> 00:08:24.030
an ecological catastrophe with his mere presence.

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:29.240
In that sense, he can be almost as dangerous
to large populations as Able.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:33.950
However, Cain’s danger to flora is only
one of his several anomalous qualities.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:38.350
Another is extraordinary mental capabilities,
and a near-perfect memory.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:43.380
His memory and ability to recall is so good,
that some Foundation personnel have suggested

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:48.400
using Cain’s mind as a kind of backup server
for the Foundation’s collective knowledge.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:53.190
But perhaps his most well-known anomalous
trait is his ability to act as a kind of immortal

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:54.690
human voodoo doll.

00:08:54.690 --> 00:09:00.130
That’s right: Any damage inflicted on Cain
causes no permanent injury to him, and is

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:02.580
reflected back on the perpetrator.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:06.790
While Cain has remarked on still being able
to feel the pain of these assaults, he’s

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:08.630
functionally immortal.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:13.380
This damage-reflecting ability has even made
performing certain kinds of tests impossible

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:17.760
- as doctors attempting to draw blood from
Cain have found that their sample was actually

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:21.940
their own blood, and their skin exhibited
the telltale bruising and puncture marks of

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:22.950
blood testing.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:28.010
But, of most interest to the Foundation right
now was the fact that Cain has shown prior

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:29.420
knowledge of Able.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.600
However, he was cagey when questioned.

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:36.440
He refused to add any additional information,
and commented that it would be best if he

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.890
and Able were never brought into contact.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:42.190
But what does “never” really mean when
you live forever?

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:46.850
Cain finally did agree to the test, and while
nobody knows what caused Cain’s change of

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:51.230
heart, the Foundation knew better than to
push him and potentially get the entire mission

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:52.230
scrapped.

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:56.760
Cain was taken from his facility, and transported
to the access point of Able’s underwater

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:57.760
prison.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:02.000
The experiment’s design was simple: Cain
would occupy a temporary residence in Able’s

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:06.620
containment facility until he next reanimated,
at which point, the interaction between them

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:08.590
would be closely observed.

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:13.090
Perhaps it would take weeks, months, or even
years before Able once again awoke and left

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:16.730
his cube, but when he did, Cain would be there.

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:21.600
Thankfully, as Cain whispered soothing words
into Able’s tomb, the resurrection took

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:22.620
only minutes.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:26.710
If you were expecting a heartwarming reunion,
think again.

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:31.390
Cain tried to apologize, but Able immediately
struck him with a decapitating blow which

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:37.010
- due to Cain's damage reflecting properties
- caused him to sever his own head instead.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:41.790
Cain remained at Able’s side as he regenerated,
and as soon as Able did he immediately tried

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:42.970
killing Cain again.

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:46.660
It went on like this again and again and again.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:53.320
It was an arduous process, and eventually,
even Able began to tire of it.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:56.060
The duo fell into a tearful embrace.

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:59.330
Able asked his brother why he killed him,
so long ago.

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:04.190
And Cain apologized, saying it was the actions
of a younger and more foolish man.

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:09.190
In that moment, the two finally reconciled,
and having fulfilled their bargain with their

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:12.490
creator, both finally crumbled into dust.

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:14.520
Peace at last.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:19.440
As we said, this didn’t happen to the Cain
and Able of our universe, but when universes

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:24.850
are more numerous than grains of sand in an
endless desert, such a thing has indeed happened

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:28.820
somewhere out there - perhaps in a kinder
universe than our own.

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:34.190
We can only hope that our Cain and Able may
someday get to meet and find the same resolution,

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:38.670
but until then, these brothers will remain
one of the most dangerous and fascinating

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.680
duos in the Foundation’s catalogue.

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:48.480
Now go check out “SCP - 087 - The Staircase”
and “SCP - 1730 - What Happened To Site-13?”

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:52.500
for more strange and tragic mysteries from
the archives of the SCP Foundation.

